            "displayName": "Tobias Bocanegra",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Tokyo"
          },
          "body": "this is not possible, because:\n* we cannot change the JCR API \n* it makes no sense to define an Iterator \"iterable\". usually collections are iterable.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=tripod",
            "name": "tripod",
            "key": "tripod",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636"
            },
            "displayName": "Tobias Bocanegra",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Tokyo"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-19T21:37:58.516+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-19T21:37:58.516+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12425847/comment/12710932",
          "id": "12710932",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dpurp",
            "name": "dpurp",
            "key": "dpurp",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "David Purpura",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "fair enough.\n\nBut, it would be nice if generics were supported, such that the following would be possible:\n\nNode root = session.getRootNode();\nfor (Node n : root.getNodes()){\n  //actions to perform\n}\n\nor the equivalent with node properties and other range iterator based implementations",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dpurp",
            "name": "dpurp",
            "key": "dpurp",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "David Purpura",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-19T22:51:26.748+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-19T22:51:26.748+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12425847/comment/12710934",
          "id": "12710934",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=alexander.klimetschek",
            "name": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "key": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443"
            },
            "displayName": "Alexander Klimetschek",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "body": "You'd have to request that for a new version of the JCR API, which is defined by a JSR standards body (https://jsr-283.dev.java.net/ and http://jcp.org/en/jsr/detail?id=283 ofr JCR 2.0). This might be something for a JCR 3.0, but I don't know anything about the plans for it and if, it won't be out before 2 or 3 years from now.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=alexander.klimetschek",
            "name": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "key": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443"
            },
            "displayName": "Alexander Klimetschek",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-19T22:55:57.243+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-19T22:55:57.243+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12425847/comment/12711059",
          "id": "12711059",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Actually, as discussed (f2f) this morning with Thomas, what we could do is add a utility class in jcr-commons that does something like this:\n\n    for (Node child : JcrUtils.childNodes(node)) {\n        // ...\n    }\n\nThe childNodes() method would be implemented like this (quick draft):\n\n    public static Iterable<Node> childNodes(final Node node) {\n        return new Iterable<Node>() {\n                public Iterator<Node> iterator() {\n                    return (Iterator<Node>) node.getNodes();\n                }\n            };\n    }\n\nWe could have similar methods for all the child node and property access methods, as well as other JCR iterators.\n\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
